# A cycle made by index writes (plan M11 5a): after `A[0] := B` and `B[0] := A`, A holds the Structure B itself and B
# holds A, one instance each -- the tree the parser built became a graph with a cycle: A[0] is B, with one field (seen),
# A[0][0] is A again, with one field (back), and A[0][0][0] is B once more (deep), so the chain of [0] does not stop at
# the first return. The dump prints the data part of main as written, so the print of the cycle by name is not checked
# here: the root Structures A and B of the fixture index_cycle_dump show it (R26, item 8).
# The declarations of ordinary Structures live in the data part of main; the root holds places and the call main().
sub: main () (
    A:
        Inner()
    B:
        Inner()
)
    A[0] := B
    B[0] := A
main()
int: seen length(main\data\A[0])
int: back length(main\data\A[0][0])
int: deep length(main\data\A[0][0][0])
